# HARD RULE — follow established UI patterns (do not invent chrome)

From the **start of every session**: before styling a new screen or sheet, **copy an existing FlareCare pattern**. Do not invent borders, card shells, or one-off chrome.

## Do this first

1. Find the closest shipped screen / component (`LogHistoryList` / `LogHistoryCard`, tracker trays, sheets, chips).
2. Match **structure + styling** (fill, radius, padding, gap) — then adapt content.
3. If unsure which pattern — ask Simon. Do **not** freestyle.

## Cards / trays / lists

- White shells and inset trays use **fill only** (`c.card`, `c.surfaceSubtle`) — **no** `borderWidth` / hairline outlines on cards, trays, chips, inputs, or sheets.
- Visual hierarchy = background contrast + spacing, not strokes.
- Reuse shared list/card components when they exist — do not hand-roll bordered “cards”.

